# Chapter data invariants

Full format spec: `docs/chapter-dsl.md`. Read it before editing any `.txt`.

## Never break line numbering

In `scripts/*.txt`, **the line number is the chapter number**. Empty lines are
real chapters with no outgoing paths (e.g. line 266 of
`T02-la-confrerie-de-nuada.txt`), and the parser keeps them on purpose.

- Never delete, insert, reorder or sort lines to "clean up" a file.
- To blank a chapter, leave the line empty. To add one, append at the end.
- Do not strip trailing whitespace in a way that removes blank lines.

## Regenerate and commit both files

`scripts/*.mermaid` are committed build artifacts that the app imports with
`?raw`. Editing a `.txt` has no visible effect until you regenerate.

```sh
cd scripts && node to-mermaid.ts
```

Run it from `scripts/`: inputs are read relative to the module URL, outputs are
written relative to the current working directory. Commit the `.txt` and the
regenerated `.mermaid` together.

## Adding a book

Register it in the `files` array of `to-mermaid.ts` (`fileName`, `id`, `name`,
`chapterToSkip`), then add a `?raw` import plus a `books` entry in
`src/pages/BookVisualizer.tsx` and the id to `BookIds` in `src/types/books.ts`.

## Two registries

`to-mermaid.ts` has its own `specialNodes` array; `src/services/chapterType.ts`
is a newer rewrite with different field names, class names and edge semantics.
Only `to-mermaid.ts` affects the generated diagrams. Changing one does not
change the other — say which you mean.

## Notes

- `scripts/` is excluded from ESLint and from `tsconfig.json`'s `include`, so
  neither `pnpm lint` nor `pnpm build` checks this code.
- An unregistered `KEY-` token crashes the generator on a non-null assertion
  with no line number in the message.
- `chapterToSkip` silently drops incoming paths to the listed chapters.
